    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s May 21st slate, **Geraldo Perdomo** emerges as our strongest play with a 68.61 efficiency score. His favorable matchup against Zach Agnos (5.15 xERA) provides the highest SP skill boost on the board (+19%), making him an essential start despite a moderate platoon disadvantage. **Tyler Freeman** and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** follow closely in the 66\u201367 range; **Freeman** benefits from a strong park factor and a soft matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez, while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a staple in the two-hole, providing stability despite facing the talented Casey Mize. We are prioritizing these bats to maximize our 5x5 categories, leaning on their expected volume in the top third of the order to compensate for any volatility.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved **Lawrence Butler**, who sits on the borderline of our \"Strong\" tier at 58.68. He narrowly earned the nod over our remaining depth options due to a significant +13% boost from his platoon dynamic against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. **Masyn Winn** presents the highest risk in the starting lineup; his score of 43.36 reflects the difficulty of facing Brady Ashcraft, combined with a negative efficiency penalty due to Ashcraft\u2019s elite catcher counterpart, which suppresses **Masyn Winn**'s stolen base potential. While we are currently waiting on official confirmation for the lineups of **Tyler Freeman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Geraldo Perdomo**, we are comfortable with these assignments; the potential for increased at-bats in the heart of the order outweighs the marginal risk of a late scratch. We continue to monitor the status of our injured anchors **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** while **Bryson Stott** and **Will Smith** remain sidelined due to team off-days, forcing us to lean heavily on the remaining active roster.",
